From 8120c3cedc689e5a145f04c841bb248703043b4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:28:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat: tool_choice none no longer returns a raw tool call as
 content (Qwen3.x)

Found by QA on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next and Qwen3.8-27B: with tools offered and
tool_choice "none", the reply's content was the raw
`<tool_call>\n<function=...>...</tool_call>` block.

Root cause: tool_choice none keeps the tools in the rendered prompt (as it
should), so the model still opens a call, but the Qwen3-Coder parser
(common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp, the route for Qwen3.5/Qwen3.8, Nemotron Nano 3
and StepFun-3.5-Flash) and the differential autoparser (Qwen3 and other
marker-based templates) fall back to a content-only parser, `content(rest())`,
under tool_choice none. Nothing stopped the opener from being sampled, and the
whole call was returned as message content.

Reproduction (CPU, Qwen3.5-0.8B-Q8_0, which shares the Qwen3.8 template route
and vocab): "What is the weather in Paris right now? Use the tool." with a
get_weather tool and tool_choice none returned
content="<tool_call>\n<function=get_weather>\n<parameter=city>\nParis\n..."
in all four of stream on/off x thinking on/off.

Fix, the same two halves as the K2-Horizon fix (fork PR #16):
- generation: common_chat_params gains `suppressed_tokens`. Under tool_choice
  none with tools offered, both parsers name the call opener (`<tool_call>`;
  the autoparser uses its grammar trigger marker), and common_chat_session bans
  it with a -inf logit bias when it is one non-normal token. A plain-text marker
  is left alone so no ordinary word piece is ever banned. The model then writes
  a text answer instead of a call it cannot make.
- parsing: the content-only parser used under tool_choice none ends the content
  at the opener and drops the rest, so a call the model still spells out (or a
  marker that could not be banned) is neither a tool call nor content.

After: tool_choice none returns plain text, no <tool_call>, finish_reason stop,
in all four modes; tool_choice auto still returns the get_weather call.

Tests (tests/test-chat.cpp): Qwen3.5 and Qwen3 parse cases with and without
reasoning, and test_tool_choice_none_suppresses_call_opener, which checks the
chat params and the session's logit bias (none vs auto, both routes), plus the
ban itself against a real Qwen GGUF when TEST_CHAT_QWEN_GGUF names one (the
repo's vocab files have no <tool_call> token).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BidfYiPxg2nUvGVowCgTPK
